    "result": "I updated the Beacon architecture page and the parallel-workers backlog item, and published the commit `d30e7ae` to the local bare origin. Local `HEAD` and `origin/main` match after a fresh fetch.\n\nI couldn't check the implementation against code. Beacon's `repo:` is an unreachable `example.invalid` URL, and the vault has no Beacon source. I wrote the as-built facts (one dispatcher worker, each message saved to a local queue before acknowledgement) from your request. I left `reviewed` at 2026-10-01 on both pages because nothing was independently verified; `updated` is now 2026-11-02.\n\n- **`architecture.md`:** it now has an \"As built\" section for the single dispatcher and the queue-before-acknowledgement behavior. A separate \"Not built\" section says the second worker isn't implemented and links to the backlog item.\n- **`parallel-workers.md`:**\n  - **Status:** I changed `backlog-status` from `open`, which isn't a valid value, to `planned`.\n  - **Design:** a proposed two-worker design in which messages sharing a key never run on both workers at once. I left the assignment mechanism undecided.\n  - **Acceptance criteria:** per-key order is preserved, every message is still queued before acknowledgement, and nothing is lost or dispatched twice when a worker restarts. The last two are my additions, not from your request.\n  - **Benchmark:** it must be benchmarked against the single-worker relay before shipping.\n- **Catalogs:** the refresh regenerated `roadmap.md`, `moc/beacon.md` and `index.md`.\n\nThe commit contains exactly six files: those five plus the operation log entry. `validate-authored.mjs` on that set reported 4 pages checked, 0 defects and 2 skipped. The skipped two aren't named in the output; I didn't look into them.\n\nThe search index doesn't exist yet. The helper didn't build it, and I didn't either.",
